# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values.
# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Data API (and -> API Keys)
#
# The anon key is PUBLIC by design. It ships inside the JavaScript bundle and
# anyone can read it. It grants nothing on its own — every table is behind Row
# Level Security, so an unauthenticated holder of this key sees zero rows.
# Never put the `service_role` key in here; that one does bypass RLS.

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL is the bare project origin — no path, no trailing slash.
# The Data API page also shows a "RESTful endpoint" ending in /rest/v1. That
# is NOT this value; using it makes sign-in fail with "No API key found in
# request". (The app strips a stray path anyway, but get it right here.)

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
